package ai

// Retained for admitted scripts and explicit primitive consumers.
const computerLegacyScriptDocumentation = `Run JavaScript in a persistent Turn-and-target namespace; save variables on globalThis. Await UI operations sequentially. This is a bounded JSON API, not Playwright or browser JavaScript.
APIs (all UI/browser calls are async):
ui.observe({root_ref?:string,limit?:1..1000,emit?:boolean,full?:boolean,screenshot?:boolean}) returns {url,title,observation:{url,title,nodes,truncated}}. emit:false keeps the tree local; full:true forces a full emitted snapshot instead of a diff.
ui.getByRole(role:string,{name?:string,exact?:boolean,root_ref?:string}) or ui.ref(ref:string) returns a locator with read(), click(), fill(text:string), press(key:string), scroll(delta_y:number,delta_x:number=0), waitFor({state:'visible'|'hidden'|'enabled',timeout_ms:0..30000}). read() returns {node}; inspect a row's subtree using ui.observe({root_ref:node.ref}). Use roles and refs from the current observation; do not infer roles from a control's business purpose. Regex names and string scroll directions are unsupported. Name matching is case-insensitive contains unless exact:true; locators require uniqueness across the complete scope even when observation is truncated. Check waitFor().state for timeout.
ui.click(x:number,y:number,image?), ui.drag(from_x,from_y,to_x,to_y,duration_ms=0,image?), ui.key(key:string), ui.screenshot(), ui.assert(condition,message?), log(...values).
Browser scroll returns {scroll_progress:{scope,measured_ref?,before,after,offset_changed,scroll_effect:"unknown",measurement:"immediate_after_dispatch"}} from the scroll() return value, not read().node. Log const r=await locator.scroll(80); log(r.scroll_progress). Offsets describe only the requested element or viewport, not a guessed wheel receiver. Measurements may be null or unchanged before animation settles; never infer failure or repeat automatically.
Browser-only locator.query({limit?:1..200,cursor?:string}) returns {items:[{ref,role,name}],total,truncated,next_cursor?,scope:'loaded_accessibility_tree'}. Count with total; narrow by role/name/root_ref. Continue next_cursor only while contents stay unchanged; virtualized unloaded rows are not included. locator.getAttribute(name) returns {attribute,value}; any exact nonempty DOM attribute name (up to 2,000 characters), subject to privacy and the 2,000-code-point value limit. attribute(name) is the scalar string|null alias. href preserves source query/fragment and relative form; URL credentials are removed with redacted:[url_credentials]. linkSummary is deprecated: it deliberately removes query/fragment; use getAttribute for exact source values.
Browser visual input: image={coordinate_space:"image_pixels",frame,document_id} from screenshot.frame_geometry. Never guess DPR. Old ui.click coordinates remain CSS viewport pixels. Image coordinates reject changed target/document/viewport; observe again. model_pixels binds optimized image coordinates on browser and native targets; image_pixels remains browser source pixels. Keys use characters or named keys joined with Alt/Control/Meta/Shift, e.g. Meta+=, Enter, ArrowDown; Equal is not a key name.
browser.navigate(url:string,options?), browser.back(options?), browser.reload(options?). Options: {wait_until:commit|domcontentloaded|load,timeout_ms:0..30000}; defaults load/20000. The wait state reached|timeout is data, not application readiness; inspect the current page without replaying navigation. Downloads: const {cursor}=await browser.downloadCursor(); await ui.getByRole('link',{name:'Export',exact:true}).click(); const result=await browser.waitForDownload({after:cursor,timeout_ms:10000}); check result.download.state==='completed'. Use {id:string} for an already identified download. Multiple new downloads are ambiguous; inspect returned downloads and choose the exact ID. Never identify a download by latest file or filename alone. Managed downloads include the saved path.
There is no setTimeout, ui.waitFor, DOM, Node, filesystem, network or raw CDP. Use locator.waitFor for conditions. Limits: 50 operations, 30 seconds, 64 MiB, 64 KiB total logs. Keep observations local with emit:false and log only selected facts or compact computed summaries; logging a complete tree may exceed the limit. SCRIPT_REFERENCE_ERROR means unavailable name; SCRIPT_TYPE_ERROR means unsupported method/type; SCRIPT_ARGUMENT_ERROR means invalid documented arguments; SCRIPT_OUTPUT_LIMIT means too much logged output. completed_actions preserves effects before failure: observe first and never repeat completed or uncertain effects automatically. A failed script loses its namespace.
Verify current URL, title and account/workspace before data collection and final conclusions. Stay within the user's requested scope. truncated and children_truncated indicate omitted observation content: narrow with root_ref; do not infer empty rows or virtualization. Report incomplete coverage explicitly.`
